  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental receipts/disbursements from p4 Total Governmental Funds column; beginning/ending fund balance p4; ending_cash = governmental funds balance sheet cash and cash equivalents 1,990,364 (p3; restricted cash 389,836 separate). Interest/dividends 65,781 printed under Other Financing Sources below total receipts, recorded as receipt outside_printed_total. Net transfers (55,111) recorded as transfers_out. Transfer cross-check: governmental funds net -55,111 = business-type transfers +2,862 (p6) + internal service fund +52,249 (p6); no hidden transfers in spending lines. Business-type from p6 total column (excludes internal service fund); beginning net position 40,160,892 as previously stated plus error correction -744,619 gives 55,265,427; no single printed total for business-type receipts/disbursements so computed. Business-type cash flows p7 total enterprise column; no noncapital financing section. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1). Taxes combined line not breakable. Recheck: the business-type 'Miscellaneous/ merchandise sales/ grants' line (p6) was split using the Statement of Activities (p2): capital grants and contributions 15,049,481 to intergovernmental/state aid (grantor not stated) and the 123,366 remainder to other (p2 shows other misc revenues 123,365; 1 rounding). Attempt 2 (2026-10-28 verifier fixes): Rent/leases 133,546 -> Rentals. Detail (user rule 2026-10-27, cities): the only supplementary schedule is the combined all-funds Budgetary Comparison Schedule (p8, fund totals only), so its lines were removed and detail is one line per individual fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4: General, Economic Development, HUD, Capital Improvement, Other Governmental Funds) and the proprietary statement (p6: Electric, Water, Gas, Sewer; Total and Internal Service columns not used, the internal service fund is outside the business-type total). Per-fund 'Miscellaneous/ merchandise sales/ grants' takes its dominant part from p2 capital grants (Electric 15,014,344 and Sewer 21,514 grants -> intergovernmental/state aid; Water and Gas mostly merchandise/misc -> Sale of Merchandise). Enterprise revenue totals are the p8 fund receipts lines, which equal the p6 column sums; Electric expenditure total 7,066,108 (p8) equals p6 operating expenses + interest; Water expenditure total computed; Gas and Sewer use p6 total operating expenses (no interest expense). Statement transfers lines are recorded as other financing per fund (governmental ones printed below Total disbursements, outside_printed_total). Read pages 1-8 of 8"
